---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { pageJsonLd, topTrail } from '../lib/seo';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/Virtual-Domain-driven-design/virtualddd.com';
const description =
  'Where AI is used on this site and where it is not: the recordings, the writing, the images, and the site itself.';

const jsonLd = pageJsonLd(Astro.site, {
  url: new URL('/ai-usage-on-this-site/', Astro.site).toString(),
  name: 'AI usage on this site',
  description,
  trail: topTrail('AI usage on this site', '/ai-usage-on-this-site/'),
});
---

<BaseLayout title="AI usage on this site — Virtual DDD" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--pink">Transparency</p>
    <h1>AI usage on this site</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-muted">
      <p>
        We use AI in some places and not in others, and we would rather tell you which is which than
        leave you guessing. Here is the whole of it.
      </p>

      <h2>The conversations are real</h2>
      <p>
        Every session and every story is a recording of people talking. None of it is generated, and
        none of the voices are synthetic. We edit the recordings in <em>Descript</em>, which uses AI
        for the tedious parts: removing the ums, tightening a long pause, cleaning up audio.
      </p>
      <p>
        We invite guests, and what they bring is theirs. We cannot tell you whether a slide they
        showed or an abstract they sent us was written with AI, and we do not ask.
      </p>

      <h2>The site is built with AI, and the code is public</h2>
      <p>
        This version of the site was designed and written with an AI coding agent, working from a
        written brief that says what the site is for and how it should behave. A person reviews every
        change and every change is signed and committed by a person. Nothing reaches the site because
        an agent decided it should.
      </p>
      <p>
        You do not have to take our word for it. The whole thing is open:
        <a href={REPO} target="_blank" rel="noopener">the source, the brief and every commit</a> are
        on GitHub, including the ones where we got it wrong and said so in the message.
      </p>
      <p>
        The brand underneath it is not ours and is not generated. The logo, the colours and the
        typography came from <a href="https://artofdesign.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Art of
        Design</a>, and the build works inside what they made.
      </p>

      <h2>How a page gets here</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you read is written and edited by us in Notion. A script reads Notion, turns each
        page into a file in the repository, and commits it. The site is then rebuilt and published
        automatically. That means the text on a page is the text somebody typed, and you can see the
        moment it changed in the commit history.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing publishes itself. A page appears here only once a human sets its status to published
        in Notion, and comes down the same way.
      </p>

      <h2>Where AI writes a first draft</h2>
      <p>
        After a story is recorded, we use AI to turn the transcript into a first draft of the written
        version and to pull out the design heuristics that came up in the conversation. Both are then
        edited by us before anything is published, and the heuristics are curated by hand: we throw
        plenty of them away.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same goes for the posts that announce a session or a story on social media. They are
        drafted automatically and saved as drafts, and one of us reads and sends them.
      </p>

      <h2>Images</h2>
      <p>
        Some images are generated: the illustrations on the heuristics and the background templates
        the story artwork is built on, both made to match our branding. Photographs of people are
        photographs of people. We are moving the generated ones over to <em>Canva</em> as we go.
      </p>

      <h2>Our own writing</h2>
      <p>
        What we write ourselves gets spell-checked and tidied with Grammarly and, now and then, a
        language model. The thinking, the opinions and the mistakes are ours.
      </p>

      <p class="ai-ask">
        If something here looks wrong, or you think we have drawn the line in the wrong place, tell
        us in <a href="https://discord.gg/tRJkcsFDKN" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord</a>. We
        would rather argue about it than get it quietly wrong.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .page { max-width: 48rem; padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-16); }
    .page h1 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-8); }
    .prose h2 { margin-top: var(--space-10); }
    .ai-ask { margin-top: var(--space-10); }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
